MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The End of Heartache and Vol. 3 felt like natural next choices because they combine heavy riffs with memorable melodies, connecting with my In Flames, Soilwork, and Disturbed listening.",
    "Ghost Reveries appealed because my recent interest in Tool makes me want to explore longer, progressive arrangements alongside heavier passages; City of Evil and Ascendancy also fit my interest in energetic, melodic guitar work."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "See You On The Other Side felt less relevant because heaviness alone is not what I want right now; melodic guitar work and progressive arrangements are stronger draws for me.",
    "Live In Texas missed my current intention to explore studio albums. Waking the Fallen, The War Within, and Curse still fit my taste, but I would prioritize my other selections during this visit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations sometimes treated an aggressive sound as enough of a connection, even though the balance of aggression, melody, and interesting arrangements matters more to me.",
    "A connection to familiar heavy rock listening did not always translate into something I wanted to explore now, especially when the recommendation was a live recording."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent Tool listening points toward an interest in progressive song structures, which helps explain why Ghost Reveries stood out so strongly.",
    "I only choose a handful of albums at a time, so passing over another relevant heavy album can mean I prefer a stronger match today, rather than that I dislike its sound."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in heavy music with melody, but some gave too little weight to progressive arrangements and my current preference for studio albums."
}
